{"id":"taanach","name":"Taanach","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:taanach"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Taanach","text":"A sandy place, an ancient royal city of the Canaanites, on the south-western border of the plain of Esdraelon, 4 miles south of Megiddo. Its king was conquered by Joshua (12:21). It was assigned to the Levites of the family of Kohath (17:11-18; 21:25). It is mentioned in the song of Deborah (Judg. 5:19). It is identified with the small modern village of Ta’annuk."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H8590","lemma":"תַּעֲנָךְ","xlit":"Taʻănâk","gloss":"Taanak or Tanak, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Taanach, Tanach","count":7,"share":0.88},{"strong":"H4023","lemma":"מְגִדּוֹן","xlit":"Mᵉgiddôwn","gloss":"Megiddon or Megiddo, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Megiddo, Megiddon","count":6,"share":0.75},{"strong":"H1052","lemma":"בֵּית שְׁאָן","xlit":"Bêyth Shᵉʼân","gloss":"Beth-Shean or Beth-Shan, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Beth-shean, Beth-Shan","count":4,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H4519","lemma":"מְנַשֶּׁה","xlit":"Mᵉnashsheh","gloss":"Menashsheh, a grandson of Jacob, also the tribe descende","kjv":"Manasseh","count":5,"share":0.63},{"strong":"H1756","lemma":"דּוֹר","xlit":"Dôwr","gloss":"Dor, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Dor","count":3,"share":0.38},{"strong":"H2991","lemma":"יִבְלְעָם","xlit":"Yiblᵉʻâm","gloss":"Jibleam, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Ibleam","count":2,"share":0.25}],"verses":["Josh.12.21","Josh.17.11","Josh.21.25","Judg.1.27","Judg.5.19","1Kgs.4.12","1Chr.7.29","Josh.17.12"],"related":[{"id":"beth-shean","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.364,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"megiddo","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.313,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"manasseh-the-tribe-of","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.03,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"beth-shean","type":"lexical","strong":"H8590","why":"both lead with תַּעֲנָךְ (H8590)"},{"id":"bileam